{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1786437435,"nonce":"PTmNXW9evkT2EkyNqD6Q6XBf+Qc=","message":"Done. `test/load/` now holds a repeatable load case with checked-in numbers (`test/load/RESULTS.md`), gated behind a `//go:build load` tag so it is runnable but never CI-blocking — a `testing.Short()` guard alone would NOT have worked, because `just test` runs without `-short`.\n\nReal numbers, 2-CPU/4 GiB colima VM, postgres:17-alpine, under concurrent load — indicative, explicitly not a contract:\n\n| case | alerts | status | ingest latency | Slack calls | rollups | storm notices | lost | dup | wedged |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| single_batch_500 | 500 | 1x202 | 23.9 ms | 4 | 2 | 0 | 0 | 0 | no |\n| chunked_batch_2200 | 2200 | 1x202 | 52.0 ms | 8 | 6 | 0 | 0 | 0 | no |\n| sustained | 3120 | 36x202, 3x503 | p50 14.1 / p99 34.8 ms | 66 | 7 | 1 of 6 storming groups | 0 | 0 | no |\n| shedding_burst | 1920 | 48x202, 251x503, ZERO 4xx | p50 3.7 / p99 102.4 ms | 51 | 49 | 0 | 0 | 0 | no |\n\n7,740 alerts total: zero lost, zero duplicated, zero wedged, every shed recovered on retry.\n\n**O(groups) holds end to end: 500 alerts produce 2 rollups (0.4%)** — under the defect 0ac132b fixed this would read ~500. The 48-batch burst is 49, i.e. O(batches x groups), never O(alerts). This is the real-Postgres counterpart to joinmany_test.go and would have caught the original defect.\n\nExactly one storm notice per channel: 6 groups entered storm mode and 6 storm notifications were recorded (the record is complete per §B.6), but exactly ONE broadcast_reply reached the channel and exactly one channel carried the storm_notice_at latch. No-loss/no-duplication is proved in both directions — 66 accepted Slack writes against 66 sent rows. Ordering gate: every thread ended last_sent_seq = next_seq - 1.\n\nTwo findings:\n1. THE SHEDDER FIRES AT MODEST SCALE, and more strongly than first thought — 3x503 on the sustained case with DEFAULT configuration, no pool shrinking. Not theoretical.\n2. oto asks for Retry-After: 10 (254 times across the run). The earlier driver's 1.5s budget was shorter than that, which is what produced its phantom 'lost alerts' — a client giving up before oto's advertised backoff, i.e. ADR 0007's five-minute Alertmanager budget in miniature. That is now a HARD ASSERTION: the driver's budget must exceed the largest ask, and the failure message says plainly that the loss is the driver's fault, not oto's.\n\nWorth watching, recorded but not asserted: **the rollup is O(groups) but the job queue is still O(alerts)** — enrich.run is 1 job/alert and notify.evaluate runs at ~2n (6,246 jobs for 3,120 alerts). On this VM that dominates drain time (91s for 2,200 alerts), not Slack. If ingest latency ever looks fine while storms feel slow, that is where to look.","files":null}]}